{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["Yehudah, you — your brothers shall yodukha — he who explains 'your brothers shall praise you' has folly in his hand. Rather, since he censured the firstborns and took the kingship from Reuben and scattered Shimon and Levi, he said to Yehudah: but you — your brothers shall give, to you — the hod of kingship, as the end of the verse proves: your father's sons shall bow to you. And similarly: ונתת מהודך עליו — give him of your authority in your lifetime. And similarly in Daniel: ולא נתנו עליו הוד מלכות. And similarly regarding Shlomo the phrase הוד מלכות is written: ויתן עליו הוד מלכות in Divrei HaYamim." "Yodukha — they shall make you king. Like yehodukha, as written: כי על כן עמים יהודוך. And similarly יושיעך ה׳ is like יהושיע. And even so, although יודוך is derived from the hod of kingship, the heh is not primary; rather it is from the truncated pattern of pa'al (פ״ע) verbs whose root letter is yod (יו״ד), like ישב יצא, which means הושיב הוציא. And similarly from ירה: בים הורה. And יורו המורים. And similarly: איש לא הונה from the root of לא תונו. And similarly one says הודו לה׳. יודו לה׳. הוגה and רחם — all of them have their root letter at their head the letter yod (יו״ד), and it sometimes falls away and the letter vav (וא״ו) comes in its place." "And they shall bow — that you shall rule over them." "Your father's sons — since they were from four mothers, he said: your father's sons. But when Yitzhak blessed Yaakov, it is written: בני אמך."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved the unnamed earlier commentator's reading as 'your brothers shall praise you' (from the root הודה, to praise/thank); Rashbam rejects this in favor of 'they shall give you הוד/authority' from the root הוד.", 1 "Rashbam's grammatical argument concerns verbs whose first root letter is י and whose הופע form (hitpa'el-like causative) alternates with a ו pattern; 'truncated pattern of pa'al verbs' renders his חטופי פ״ה פעל, where פ״ה = peh-heh verbs (first root letter) and פעל = the binyan name."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:48.182508156Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}